{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared contract between the two implementations of the Yaniv discard rules:",
    "  server  - src/main/java/shop/abwork/yanif/game/validator/CardCombinationValidator.java",
    "  client  - frontend/src/utils/yanivRules.ts",
    "The client copy exists so the UI can grey out illegal selections without a round",
    "trip. It is not authoritative, but if the two drift the UI either offers moves the",
    "server rejects or blocks legal ones.",
    "",
    "Both are tested against this file:",
    "  RulesContractTest.java              (./mvnw test -Dtest=RulesContractTest)",
    "  yanivRules.contract.test.ts         (cd frontend && npm test)",
    "",
    "sequenceValues pins the SEQUENCE ladder, which is deliberately different from the",
    "scoring values in handScores: J/Q/K are 11/12/13 here but all score 10, and Ace is",
    "1 or 14. Mixing the two is the easiest mistake to make in this codebase.",
    "",
    "Add a case here when you change a rule. Ranks: ACE TWO..TEN JACK QUEEN KING.",
    "Suits: HEARTS DIAMONDS CLUBS SPADES."
  ],
  "combinations": [
